  "id": "BIT-sqlite-2026-119374",
  "summary": "SQLite before 3.54.0 Heap Buffer Overflow via FTS5 fts5DoSecureDelete()",
  "details": "SQLite before 3.54.0 built with FTS5 contains a heap buffer overflow in fts5DoSecureDelete() that allows attackers to write past the leaf page buffer via crafted footer key offsets. Attackers can supply a database file with a corrupted FTS5 index that, when deleted from with secure-delete enabled, corrupts heap memory and crashes the application.",
